<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42989" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scirpĭcŭlus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sirp-</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">surp-</span></b> ), a, um
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Adj., <i>of</i> or <i>made of
				rushes.</i> So with falces (their use is unknown),
					<i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 11, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 22, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. L. L. 5, § 137</span></i>
			Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fiscella,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Exod. 2, 3</span></i>
			.—More freq., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scirpĭcŭlus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sirp-, surp-</span></b> ), i,
				m., <i>a basket made of rushes</i>, <i>a rush-basket</i>: surpiculi olerorum, Lucil. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 490, 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 2, 2, 10</span></i>; Col. poët. 10, 305; <i><span class="en">Prop. 4</span></i>
			(5), 2, 40: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piscarii,</span>”
				<i>wears</i>, <i>weels</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. 4, 2, 36</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
